        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(bedrock): enable prompt caching for Nova models",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #29707. Amazon Nova generation models on Bedrock were still treated as unsupported non-Anthropic models, so OpenClaw forced `cacheRetention: \"none\"` and never emitted Bedrock `cachePoint` blocks for Nova requests.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAWS documents explicit prompt caching support for Amazon Bedrock models, including Nova generation models: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-caching.html\n\nThis change teaches the Bedrock provider to recognize Nova Micro, Lite, Pro, Premier, and Nova 2 Lite refs, lets direct Nova requests keep their explicit cache settings, and keeps the existing no-cache fallback for unsupported non-Anthropic Bedrock models. For Nova, `cacheRetention: \"long\"` emits the default Bedrock cache point without reusing Claude's `ttl: \"1h\"` field.\n\nNova eligibility now has a single owner: the Amazon Bedrock provider normalization seam. The provider sets generic runtime compatibility metadata for eligible Nova models, while the shared agent cache-retention path only consumes that capability and contains no Bedrock model IDs or Nova-family matcher.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can enable prompt caching for Bedrock Nova text models without hitting the previous runtime no-cache override. Unsupported non-Anthropic Bedrock models, such as Mistral, continue to be protected from unsupported cache metadata.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1` on all 9 follow-up files\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint` on all 9 follow-up files\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/prompt-cache-retention.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/extra-params.cache-retention-default.test.ts` (38 tests passed)\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/amazon-bedrock/index.test.ts extensions/amazon-bedrock/stream.runtime.test.ts` (100 tests passed)\n- `node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/model.test.ts -t \"uses provider-normalized model ids for OpenRouter transport\"` (1 passed, 128 skipped)\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` (passed)\n- Fresh independent autoreview after addressing its integration-coverage finding: no actionable findings\n\nThe local extension and core-test `tsgo` lanes produced no diagnostics but exceeded 6-7 minute local timeouts. The corresponding GitHub checks are running on the pushed head.\n\nLive Bedrock Nova request proof was not run because this contributor does not have a usable Nova-enabled AWS account. Redacted live `Converse` or `ConverseStream` proof showing accepted cache points and `cacheReadInputTokens` / `cacheWriteInputTokens` is still needed before merge.\n\nAI-assisted contribution.\n",
        "branch": "fix/bedrock-nova-prompt-cache",
